# Grok / AI

## Entry points

| Trigger | Path |
|---------|------|
| `@mention` or reply to bot | `ApiManager.routeMention` → `GrokManager.askFromMention` |
| Context menu Ask Cyan | slash route → `GrokManager.askAboutMessage` |
| `/draw` | slash route → `GrokManager.draw` |
| Context menu Draw | slash route → modal → `GrokManager.completeDrawFromMessage` |

## Layering

- `GrokManager` — prompts, reply-chain / channel context, Discord replies
- `GrokUtil` — xAI HTTP (chat Responses API + image generate/edit)
- `grok-prompt.ts` — `CYAN_SYSTEM_PROMPT` and `GrokPrompt` shape
- `grok-routes.ts` — thin handlers only

## Conventions

- Inject `Config`; require `XAI_API_KEY` and throw `BotError` if missing
- Keep context limits as coded (reply chain max 10; channel msgs max 15 × 300 chars; chat images max 3)
- Reply-chain fetches stay in the invoking channel — do not follow forwards or other cross-channel references
- Chat may call client image tools only when the user explicitly asks to draw/edit
- Do not invent new AI entry points outside mention/reply, Ask Cyan, and `/draw` without updating `ApiManager` / `ApiV1`
